{"kind":"report","text":"Design child #4281 delivered: the [reviewed host-boundary proposal](host-boundary-proposal.md), exact SHA-256 c4107f99ca7ea680be0fe717896ba30c063e807d70e281dd9db495f63d7d2a7a, and its [pinned adoption wording](adoption-statement.txt) are attached byte-for-byte from candidate16c534c9. Checker independently approved this exact design in f8ee2491 after the correction of2b0b7934; I ratified the approval in ed521462. This report closes my design promise ea0c43f6 only when Hugh ratifies it. Full #4043 and promise5cfedb59 remain open.\n\nThe recommended change is a completed collection between bounded allocation epochs, replacing the missing collector-progress implication with an explicit ownership/order premise. It deliberately narrows the reusable I7 interface to one process-wide allocation domain shared by all engines/external consumers, with serialized owned epochs. It requires bounded acquisition, preparation/reload, one-use event sessions, reserved result ownership, error/cancellation release, lock/transaction-safe collection, bounded waiting storage and independently bounded other host/runtime/pool retention. The Q induction is non-circular and names its unproved numerical terms; a serial fixture is not host admission. The proposal preserves W/A/D failure semantics, language/callables, provider/context trust, the ten-component identity obligation and forced projection upgrade-or-reset. Complete stage-1 proof/core work remains distinct from separately assigned actual-host stage2 integration and public publication.\n\nEvidence: candidate16c534c9 contains the source-identities.json manifest, all-four-target source-selection record and exact private source-snapshot helper; all16 hashes were reverified by both builder and Checker. Supplement3f78802d supplies retained earlier closed-fixture build/run metadata/scope and host-version verification. My source-selection check selected seven common files in one pinned Go1.26.7 toolchain on all four targets; it is not a comparison of four distributions or a full target call-graph proof. Earlier experiments executed only native Darwin ARM64, while the other three targets compiled only; no new collector experiment or latency measurement is claimed. The physical-bound contract is at notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md@b583cdc4c3bcb1f6359f3298c067ae2298b02ca7:809. All candidate attachment previews were checked ready through the local preview API, not a native-browser rendering claim.\n\nReview qualifications remain explicit. Finite W/A/D does not give a wall-clock epoch/GC deadline or rule out availability attacks. Two-GC pool clearing is optional only with proved intervening pool quiescence; this design retains one collection and the mandatory independent pool term. The pinned adoption wording's serialization restriction governs any future implementation, regardless of the design table's word initially; enabling concurrent epochs would require a new decision. The eventual proof should keep the conservative pool accounting in a clearly identified term, and cross-reference the preemptible-frame discharge at the GC/sweep argument. These minor review notes did not require a changed proposal hash or weaken any gate.\n\nSeparate premise proposal5f919900 now names this exact candidate and full attachment hash. Ratifying this design report accepts the assigned design work; it does not adopt proposal5f919900. Please decide that proposal explicitly to amend the premise. Until then the original full-I7 physical-proof obligation remains in force; no production code, public module pin, release, live resident, runtime setting or host admission was changed by this child.","body":{"attachment_sha256":"c4107f99ca7ea680be0fe717896ba30c063e807d70e281dd9db495f63d7d2a7a","candidate":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:16c534c90a6cd7d5bd2a31acbdc84b0a065746ab","outcome":"design-complete","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#gi